Z||000020||Ken Wittlief||07-12-2001||11:02 AM||||If your stat is working correctly and your engine is at the proper temp, then make a mental note of where 'normal' is for your dash gauge <P>  and dont worry about it unless the gauge climbs up way past that someday<P> your gauge is simply off- it doesnt really matter if its not accurate, as long as its consistant.<P>  unless its all over the place and is differnt everyday - dont worry about it - spend your time and money on something that is functional<P>  if anyone asks you about it, tell them thats degrees Centiheight, or Faragrade.||||reg||1
